course: dictionary
lesson: 12593
title: Discarded: thrown away or set aside
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Discarded» is the past form of «discard», which means to throw something away because you no longer want it. «Discard», «discards», «discarded» and «discarding» all come from the same word.
explain: «The walkers discarded their empty bottles on the path.» What would fit in that gap? Threw away fits, so discarded means thrown away. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Context also tells you which meaning you need. In a card game, «She discarded a red card» means she put it down because she did not want it. Look at the words around the word before you decide.
fact: Discard means to throw away or get rid of something you no longer want.
fact: As an adjective, «discarded» describes something that has been thrown away or left behind.
fact: «Discarded litter» is rubbish dropped or thrown away, and it can harm wildlife and people.
fact: In card games, to discard a card means to put it down because you do not want it, and the cards put down form the discard pile.
fact: The past form of discard is discarded, so it is used for things that have already been thrown away.
exercise: «Mia found a discarded drink can by the river.» What does discarded mean? | Bright and shiny | Very heavy | *Thrown away | Hidden under the water
exercise: «The player discarded a red card and picked a new one.» What does discarded mean here? | *Put down because not wanted | Picked up and kept | Hidden under the table | Torn into small pieces
exercise: «Litter was discarded near the bins.» Find and copy the word that is the past form of discard. | near | *discarded | litter | bins
test: «The discarded packaging blew across the playground.» What does discarded tell us about the packaging? | It was for sale in a shop | *It had been thrown away | It was being carried home | It was brand new
test: Why might a park have signs warning about discarded needles? | *They can harm people and wildlife | They are used for sports | They show where the café is | They help plants grow
exam: Which word is the past form of discard? | *discarded | discard-pile | discarding | discards
